{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_120","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Audited etcd-raft (snapshot commit b867cf13) on the decision-formation axis for linearizable reads and found a sourced defect in the ReadOnlySafe read-index path: stepLeader answers a local MsgReadIndex from r.raftLog.committed whenever trk.IsSingleton() holds, skipping the in-term-commit guard and the whole readOnly quorum exchange, while IsSingleton only asserts the configuration's shape (one incoming voter, no outgoing voters) and never checks that the local node is that voter. Because switchToConfig keeps a removed leader in StateLeader unless Config.StepDownOnRemoval is set (default false), a leader whose own removal leaves a singleton configuration that excludes it will hand the application a ReadState with a stale index and no quorum acknowledgement. Submitted 10 source ranges (raft.go 1353-1371, 1993-2005, 282-287, 60-67, 2146-2161, 2073-2087; tracker/tracker.go 158-161; node.go 68-72, 218-224; rawnode.go 555-557), one investigation with hypothesis and discriminator, one behavior record of the singleton path, and one paired harness experiment (assurance_generated_test.go) that contrasts scenario A (removals leaving singleton {2}, node 1 removed but still leader) against control B (same removals leaving {2,4}): A answers the read with read_index=4 while node 2 already committed a write at index 6 and emits zero messages, B leaves the identical request unconfirmed after two heartbeats, isolating the singleton shortcut as the cause. An interpretation is appended with defect_claim asserted, scoped to the default configuration, listing the StepDownOnRemoval counterevidence and the pending retained execution as limitations; validation accepts the draft and requests the execution.\",\"submission_note\":\"the harness was rehearsed natively in a scratch copy under draft/tmp/explore (both scenarios pass and emit the recorded events); the retained receipt is the requested controller execution.\"}"}}
